hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16178","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me that al-Husayn ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Lubabah informed him that Abu Lubabah Abd al-Mundhir, when Allah forgave him, said: O Messenger of Allah, of my repentance to Allah Almighty is that I abandon the home of my people and dwell with thee, and strip myself of my wealth as charity to Allah Almighty and to His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The third suffices thee."
